      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes a mechanism that provides transactional semantics for file writes without needing a database. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core Function:**\nThe guarded write journal records the prior state of any file before the guarded tool executor overwrites it \u2014 storing either the file\u0027s previous content or noting that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback on Failure:**\nIf the agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, and deleting any newly created files.\n\n**All-or-Nothing Semantics:**\nThis gives each run atomicity \u2014 either all writes succeed together, or they all roll back \u2014 without requiring a traditional database transaction. The journal itself acts as the transaction log, kept in memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Query Agent Exception:**\nThe Query agent (which includes this wiki query system) never uses the rollback path since it has no write capability at all, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5355,
      "output_tokens": 241
    }
